<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Key Takeaways</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Quick answer:</strong> For coat closet organization, keep only in-season coats on the rod, one or two per person, and give each zone one job: baskets on the top shelf, shoes on the floor and small items on the door. Clean off-season coats before storing them.</li>


<li>Keep only in-season coats on the rod, one or two per person, and store the rest.</li>



<li>Give each zone one job: baskets up top, coats in the middle, shoes on the floor, small items on the door.</li>



<li>Clean coats before storing them for the season and use breathable garment bags.</li>
</ul>



